## RMS (remote monitoring system) 

defination:
RMS in locomotive stands for Remote Monitoring System. It's a system that monitors a locomotive's status and faults in real time and sends the information to a base station. 

working :
1.An RMS unit is connected to the locomotive's computer, GPS receiver, and GSM/CDMA communication devices 

2.The unit continuously monitors the locomotive's internal status 
3.When it detects a fault or alert, it sends the information to a base station server 
4.The RMS unit can also be used as an emergency voice communication device for the driver 

what it monitors :
Temperature
High voltage
Software version
Isolation

what it does:
The RMS sends the information to a base station server in real time 
The RMS can send alerts to concerned authorities via email or SMS 
The RMS can provide a map view of the location of all locomotives fitted with RDS 

