## what is MVB(Multifunction vehicle bus)
The MVB (Multifunction Vehicle Bus) protocol operates as a communication system primarily used in railway applications, 
where a designated "master" device controls data transmission to multiple "slave" devices within a train by sending periodic frames that define specific time slots for each slave to send their data, ensuring real-time and deterministic communication with a fixed data rate, 
typically utilizing a single master-to-multiple slave communication structure; 

it offers two access modes: periodic (for regularly polled data) and sporadic (for event-based data transmission) to manage different types of information on the bus


