Breakdown of your Chain:
LCDIF2 (Display Controller): The internal engine that generates the raw pixels and timing (the 1024x768 @ 75MHz you configured).
LDB (LVDS Display Bridge): The internal SoC logic that takes those pixels and formats them into the VESA-24 bit-stream.
LDB PHY (Physical Layer): The actual hardware pins and high-speed differential drivers inside the i.MX8M Plus.

